<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Trimmer / AOT preservation roots for the definition layer.

  The definition graph (FormSchema, TableSchema, FormLayout, the *Settings family,
  LanguageResource and their nested collections) is transported over the JSON-RPC wire
  as an XML string and reconstructed ON THE CLIENT via XmlCodec.Deserialize<T>. The only
  callers of the parameterless constructors, public property setters and strongly-typed
  collection Add(T) members are XmlSerializer's reflection, so a trimmer that processes
  this assembly removes them as unused. At runtime that would surface as the misleading
  "XmlSerializeErrorDetails, 2, 2" (line 2, column 2 is the root element opening; the XML
  is fine, the type metadata was trimmed).

  That happens only when this assembly is actually trimmed: under TrimMode=full or
  NativeAOT. Polhem.Definition is not marked IsTrimmable, so the SDK default partial trim
  of the iOS, Mac Catalyst and Android heads copies it untouched (measured 2026-09-26),
  and this file changes nothing there. Full trim and NativeAOT are unsupported because the
  System.Text.Json envelope breaks under both (POLHEM9004 in
  buildTransitive/Polhem.Definition.targets warns about them); this descriptor keeps the
  XML half working under them all the same.

  This descriptor is embedded as the logical resource "ILLink.Descriptors.xml" so the
  trimmer auto-applies it for EVERY downstream consumer of the Polhem.Definition package -
  external framework users building trimmed/AOT mobile apps inherit the fix without
  re-deriving their own linker file.

  This is the broad "bottom layer" root (the definition type hierarchy is polymorphic and
  subtype-dense, so a per-type DynamicallyAccessedMembers pass is error-prone here). It can
  be narrowed later once the exact reflected surface is pinned down on a physical device.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="Polhem.Definition">
    <type fullname="*" preserve="all" />
  </assembly>

  <!--
    The definition collections derive from the base collection types in Polhem.Core; the
    reflection-only serializer walks their inherited construct / add / enumerate members.
  -->
  <assembly fullname="Polhem.Core">
    <type fullname="Polhem.Core.Collections.*" preserve="all" />
  </assembly>
</linker>
